# Accessibility (RealmsRPG)

Target: **WCAG 2.2 Level AA** on all UI work.

When **creating or editing** UI:

1. **Contrast:** Semantic tokens (`text-text-primary`, `text-text-secondary`). Prefer theme-aware status/archetype tokens: `text-success-fg`, `text-danger-fg`, `text-warning-fg`, `text-info-fg`, `text-power-fg`, `text-martial-fg` (not numbered ramp + ad-hoc `dark:`). Use `text-text-muted` **on its own** — do not add `dark:text-text-secondary`; the two tokens resolve to the same colour in dark mode by design, so the override is dead CSS (see `DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` § "Muted vs secondary text"). See `ACCESSIBILITY.md` / `DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`.

2. **Buttons:** Discernable text; icon-only need `aria-label`.

3. **Form controls:** `<label htmlFor>` or `aria-label`.

4. **Headings:** No skip (h1 → h2 → h3).

5. **Modals:** `title` or `titleA11y`.

6. **Touch targets:** assign a tier from `MOBILE_UX.md` / ADR-0023 (Primary 48 / Standard 44 / Dense 32+expanded hit). Do not apply a blanket 44×44 to every control.

7. **Target size (2.2):** Interactive elements must meet WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.8 (Target Size minimum — 24×24 CSS px, or inline/spacing exception). Dense tier (32px painted + expanded hit) satisfies this on coarse pointer; verify compact fine-pointer controls meet 2.5.8 via size or the spacing exception.

8. **Focus not obscured (2.2):** Focused elements must not be entirely hidden by sticky headers, footers, or overlays (SC 2.4.11). Ensure scroll-margin / padding accounts for fixed chrome.

9. **Images:** Decorative → `alt=""`; meaningful → descriptive alt.

10. Fix `jsx-a11y` lint violations.
